# ── Secrets & runtime state — NEVER commit ──
config.json
config.json.tmp
sessions.json
sessions.json.tmp
# LEGACY: state.json was the removed Telegram bot's state (docs/adr/0006). Drop it once no node has one.
state.json
state-web.json
model-health.json
model-review.json
member-quota.json
# Claude sign-in: the long-lived token (lib/claude-token.mjs) and the watchdog's state (lib/claude-auth.mjs)
claude-token
claude-auth.json
agentmail.json*
*.log

# ── Personal data — every user's private workspace ──
# workspace/ is the owner's; workspace-<id>/ are family members'.
# Only workspace.example/ (a sanitized template) is committed.
workspace/
workspace-*/
*.deleted-*

# ── EXCEPT the owner's apps, which are CODE ──────────────────────────────────
# 21 apps, ~670KB of HTML + meta.json, existed on exactly one disk. The data they
# hold does NOT live here — the broker namespaces it to workspace/data/<slug>/
# (~64MB), which stays ignored along with conversations, journal, health and
# uploads. So this tracks the dev work and none of the contents.
#
# ALLOWLIST, deliberately: re-including the directory wholesale would commit
# whatever an app or a future feature decides to write beside its own code. Only
# the two files an app is made of are un-ignored, and test/apps-tracked.test.mjs
# fails if a tracked app ever carries anything else, or anything personal.
#
# MEMBERS' apps stay ignored. workspace-<id>/apps belongs to that person, and a
# child's app is more likely to be personal than the owner's. Their call, not this
# repo's.
!workspace/
workspace/*
!workspace/apps/
workspace/apps/*
!workspace/apps/*/
workspace/apps/*/*
!workspace/apps/*/index.html
!workspace/apps/*/meta.json

node_modules/
.DS_Store
certs/
*.crt
*.key

# The curated shelf IS source, not runtime state. It holds the apps that ship with superelf —
# the ones every node gets, the way a note pad ships with an OS — and promote() is the publish
# step, not a build artifact. Tracking it gives /changelog a real history to diff, makes each
# promote a reviewable commit, and means a fresh clone comes with the apps instead of an empty
# shelf. The one thing still ignored is the undo buffer: .versions/ is runtime, and git is
# already the better history.
shared-apps/.versions/

# panote-ocr: the Vision CLI is compiled on the node from its .swift (lib/note-ocr.mjs ensureBuilt)
tools/panote-ocr/build/

# ── Public demo (ops/demo): secrets and the data disk, never committed ──
ops/demo/.env
ops/demo/data/
ops/demo/data.img
ops/demo/.rebuild.lock

# First-run owner setup code (lib/setup-code.mjs) — a live credential
setup-code

# ── Private overlay (docs/repos.md): laid onto a checkout by the overlay's overlay.sh, never
# committed here. Generic patterns only, so this file names nothing personal. An overlay APP
# carries its own `.gitignore` of `*` (nested rules win over the `!workspace/apps/` above).
/privacy-terms.txt
/ops/private/
/docs/private-*.md
/test/private-*.test.mjs

# Written by the VM deploy (the deployed commit, lib/buildid.mjs readRevision); never committed
/REVISION
